#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
tools/t [LEVEL | CHECK ...] [options]: the phone's tests, as short as they can be and no shorter.

Levels (each a list of checks, run in ONE boot; the boot is the floor: ~50 s to a settled SpringBoard):
  host      host-side checks only (no phone): syntax, self-tests, builds that are stale. Seconds.
  quick     boot pods                       a change to userland or rendering: boots, App Library pods are lit (~75 s)
  gfx       boot pods frames                + frame pacing of the usual gestures (~110 s)
  power     boot frames sleep frames        sleep/wake: deep sleep entered and left, frame pacing the same after it (~120 s)
  display   boot frames sleep1              display, GPU, refresh: pacing, one short sleep, no fallback to autorefresh
  full      boot pods frames sleep frames sleep_rapid frames powerd idle   extended regression: only when a change is
                                            architectural, a failure is intermittent, or before a final check (~6 min)
Checks may be named instead of a level:  tools/t boot sleep

  boot        the system reaches a settled SpringBoard (CPU idle, not by a fixed wait), with no panic
  pods        the App Library's pods are lighter than their wallpaper (a screenshot, tools/look/check.py)
  frames      the usual gestures once (~14 s); a second `frames` after a `sleep` is compared with the first
  sleep       2 sleeps of 3 s from the kernel's own timer: each asserted (the wake came from the timer, the continuous
              clock ran 3 s, mach time stood still, all but 2 cores off), then the screen woken and unlocked
  sleep1      one such sleep
  sleep_rapid 5 sleeps of 2 s in a row
  powerd      one sleep of 15 s woken through powerd (IOPMSchedulePowerEvent): the iOS wake path itself
  darkwake    a dark (timer) wake, then the lock button: the screen has to light
  idle        45 s untouched, then the clocks and the display's state are read

Options:  --no-run  host checks and builds only    --keep  leave userland/rc.jobs.t     --max N  seconds the run may take
Every phase is timed and written to logs/t-<time>.txt. Needs the phone in the loader (xl state), or in fastboot.
A boot that does not reach a settled SpringBoard in 100 s without its log growing is stopped and its evidence printed:
it is not retried (look at the log first). Exit status 0 when every check passed.
"""
